<title>FRANCE: French consumer prices rose 0.2-0.3 pct in October.</title>
<headline>French consumer prices rose 0.2-0.3 pct in October.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following provisional data:</p>
<p>				    Oct	   Sept     Oct 1995</p>
<p> Month-on-month inflation  0.2-0.3	 0.4	  0.1</p>
<p> Year-on-year inflation    1.7-1.8	 1.6	  1.8</p>
<p> CPI Index (base 1990)   114.2-114.3   114.0	112.3</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following breakdown of the consumer price index for all households in mainland France, base 1990.</p>
<p>     Category		  Weight(pct) index  1-mo   3-mo  yr/yr</p>
<p> Food excluding tobacco	 20.17    106.6   0.2   -0.8    1.1</p>
<p> Private-sector manufactures  33.05    109.2   0.4    1.0    0.8</p>
<p> Private-sector services	19.76    125.0  -0.2   -0.2    2.0</p>
<p> Energy				8.25    114.1   1.6    3.0    6.4</p>
<p> Public services ex energy     6.58    126.6  -0.2   -0.9    1.1</p>
<p> Rent, water			 6.55    129.6   0.1    0.5    2.5</p>
<p> Health spending		   5.64    110.0   0.0    0.0    0.9</p>
<p> Total excluding tobacco	98.06    113.4   0.3    0.4    1.7</p>
<p>Cumulative inflation in the first 10 months of 1996 was 1.5 to 1.6 percent, INSEE said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 53 81</p>
</text>
